Represents each individual product or service line in a Purchase Order / RFQ, containing quantity, unit price, taxes, and delivery details.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Define ordered items with expected receipt date
Support 3-way matching (PO → Receipt → Vendor Bill)
Calculate line and order totals (untaxed, tax, total)
Generate stock moves for incoming products
Handle partial deliveries and remaining quantities
Purchase reporting and spend analysis per product/supplier
Blanket orders and framework agreements

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent)
Key Fields:
order_id → purchase.order (required, parent)
product_id → product.product, product_qty (float)
price_unit (monetary), discount (if installed)
taxes_id (Many2many to account.tax)
date_planned, qty_received, qty_invoiced, qty_to_invoice
product_uom → uom.uom
Computed: price_subtotal, price_total, price_tax

Critical Hooks: onchange_product_id, _compute_amount, _prepare_stock_move, _compute_qty_received, _compute_qty_invoiced
Security: Inherited from parent purchase.order

RAG Routing Keywords:
purchase order line, PO line, purchase line, RFQ line, vendor order line, procurement line, purchase order detail, ordered quantity, purchase price, purchase product line, receipt line
Related Models (most joined):

purchase.order (parent)
product.product / product.template
stock.move / stock.picking (incoming)
account.move.line (vendor bill matching)
res.partner (via order)
uom.uom
account.tax

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
purchase.order.line is the child model of purchase.order storing each purchased item with product_id, product_qty, price_unit, taxes_id, date_planned, qty_received, and qty_invoiced. It drives stock move creation, vendor bill matching (3-way), partial deliveries, line amount calculations, and is the core transactional detail used across Purchasing, Inventory, and Accounting in Odoo.